  "ncbi_key_present": true,
  "disclosures": [
    "PubMed receives the question as typed, which is the naive baseline of Figure 1a. The informed baseline, the question's distinctive content words combined with AND, is measured separately by probe-coverage-and-fair-pubmed.mjs and is the fair comparison.",
    "Arms are run as separate passes so each is paced by its own endpoint limit. Every arm sees the identical question set; only the wall-clock interleaving differs.",
    "The 120-target subset is a re-measurement of already-published figures. Any difference is drift in the third-party indexes between runs, and is reported rather than reconciled.",
    "5 targets store publisher page furniture instead of an abstract and cannot be retrieved from a paraphrase by meaning. They are retained so the two halves stay comparable, and a sensitivity analysis excluding them is reported alongside."
  ],
